# Sample Kconfig stanza for the Realtek RTL8125 Rust driver. The
# block below is the stanza you would copy into
# `drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Kconfig` when integrating this driver
# into a kernel source tree. Out-of-tree builds use the top-level
# `Makefile`; this file exists for upstream-readiness review only.

config RTL8125_RUST
	tristate "Realtek RTL8125 2.5 Gigabit Ethernet support (Rust)"
	depends on PCI && RUST
	select MII
	select PHYLIB
	select REALTEK_PHY
	help
	  Say Y here if you have a Realtek RTL8125 2.5 Gigabit Ethernet
	  PCIe adapter whose hardware revision is listed in this driver's
	  supported-chip table, and want to test this driver instead of the
	  in-tree r8169 driver.

	  This driver is written predominantly in Rust, with a thin
	  C bridge ("cshim") for kernel networking APIs that have no
	  safe-Rust abstraction yet. It is a Rust-for-Linux netdev
	  prototype; the in-tree r8169 driver also covers RTL8125 hardware
	  and is the default choice for production deployments.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here. The module
	  will be called r8125_rust.

	  See Documentation/networking/device_drivers/realtek/r8125_rust.rst
	  for module parameters, supported chips, and limitations.
